#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below), f 64;
#X obj 60 670 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 694 0: signal (mono) \; 1: events: choke \, done \, value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 754 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 778 bang \, <1-127>: trigger \, the number is the velocity \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. ptch 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; defaults \, reset: default controls \, restart the voice \; level <0-8>: output gain \, default 1 \; get <control>: reply 'value <control> <v>' on outlet 1 \; print: voice \, controls and sample rate to the Pd window \; choke \, chokems <ms>: fade the voice out \, default 3 ms \; dump: send all controls to outlet 1 as 'dump trxcb v0 ..' \; dump trxcb v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only), f 64;
#X obj 60 966 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 990 0 ptch (100) Controls the basic pitch. \; 1 dec (50) Controls the decay time. \; 2 enh (127) Enhances the body of the sound. \; 3 damp (127) Dampens the decay part. \; 4 tone (0) Changes tonal quality. \; 5 bump (0) Adds a pitchshift at the start of the sound., f 64;
#X obj 60 1114 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Choke 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1138 Outlet 1 sends 'choke' at every trigger. Connect it to the \; inlet of another voice to cut that voice off \, e.g. \; [trxch~] outlet 1 -> [trxoh~] inlet., f 64;
#X obj 60 1214 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ steps 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1238 Per-step values: connect the voice to [skpreset name] \; (outlet 1 -> inlet 0 \, outlet 0 -> voice inlet). A slot \; number 0-15 then recalls and keeps the controls for a step. \; More in skpreset-help.pd (click to open)., f 64;
